  "summary": "Uncertainty-mode verification (strictness: lenient, threshold 0.30) of 44 snippets (9 sections, 14 equations, 11 figures, 10 table blocks). One high-confidence error was confirmed: the paper attributes scene-depth estimation to 'DepthAnything-V2 [40]', but reference [40] is Restormer (a CVPR 2022 image-restoration paper), and the depth-estimation paper (Depth Anything V2) is not cited anywhere — a clear citation/attribution mismatch requiring correction. All 14 equations were checked and contain no critical algebraic errors (the max() losses in Eqs. 10/12 operate on 1-channel IR vs 3-channel VI tensors, a dimensional ambiguity resolved in practice by broadcasting, not flagged under lenient strictness). Quantitative tables are internally consistent: ControlFusion's claimed SOTA on SD/VIF/Qabf matches Table 1, Table 6's 'Ours' row matches Table 2, and Table 8's percentage shares (55.9% params, 0.81% / 7.5% FLOPs) match the text. Cross-section check found no macro-level contradictions. Non-blocking notes: (1) YOLOv8 is cited as [26], the 2016 YOLO paper by Redmon et al. — common practice but technically a misattribution since YOLOv8 is an Ultralytics model; (2) RoadScene is cited inconsistently as [36] and [35], though both FusionDN and U2Fusion are accepted citations for that dataset; (3) Table 2's comparison gives ControlFusion a pre-enhancement stage that competitors lack — disclosed by the authors, so it limits but does not invalidate the comparative claims; (4) the DDL-12 counts (2,050 source images vs ~52,800 claimed pairs) are not fully reconciled with 12 degradations x 4 levels, but the construction is under-specified and was not treated as a confirmed error.",
